# Filter Hz 1.3.0: two kHz values locked side by side keep their boxes apart. Track HPF 86 and
# LPF 0 (the corner for 86 + 0); trig 1 held in GRID RECORDING, one nudge each, which locks the
# shown value. Expected 2.17kHz and 2.21kHz, each in its own box with a black column between
# them and a pixel of white each side of both texts (the pair whose boxes touched before 1.3.0's box move).
# Ends by tapping T1 in GRID RECORDING, which takes the lock trig off, and puts HPF 38, LPF 40
# back. Needs step 1 of the FX track's pattern empty at the start.
name: filter-hz-khz-pair
state: changes
# FX is a toggle (pressed on the FX track it goes back to the drum track), so BD is selected first.
hold TRK
key BD
release TRK
key FX
key SRC
wait 3500
cc 20 86
cc 21 0
wait 300
key RECORD
hold T1
nudge E +1
nudge F +1
wait 750
screen pair
expect pair == ref region 0 40 128 15
release T1
wait 300
key T1
wait 300
key RECORD
cc 20 38
cc 21 40
